l-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i555d70cce26d468ca0c3486d4ca97e78_D20210101-20211230" decimals="-5" name="us-gaap:DistributionMadeToLimitedLiabilityCompanyLLCMemberCashDistributionsDeclared" format="ixt:fixed-zero" scale="6" id="f-703">&#8212;</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"></td></tr></table></ix:continuation></div><div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-indent:29.25pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Due to the adverse impacts of the COVID-19 Pandemic on the Company&#8217;s operations, the Company generated negative available cash by NCM LLC to its related party founding members and NCM, Inc. for the nine months ended September 29, 2022 of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="id6d0f06d5bbc48898b39a7d15c5eafa4_D20211231-20221229" decimals="-5" name="ncmi:NegativeDistributionsMadeToLimitedLiabilityCompany" scale="6" id="f-704">39.4</ix:nonFraction> million (including negative $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="id2073b0673674fbebfa3da56a824cee0_D20211231-20221229" decimals="-5" name="ncmi:NegativeDistributionsMadeToLimitedLiabilityCompany" scale="6" id="f-705">10.5</ix:nonFraction> million for Cinemark, negative $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="ibd3e5db1d931423ca816d428e60ac6c1_D20211231-20221229" decimals="-5" name="ncmi:NegativeDistributionsMadeToLimitedLiabilityCompany" scale="6" id="f-706">9.3</ix:nonFraction> million for Regal and negative $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i09aeacb6ca3141cfb17c300636add840_D20211231-20221229" decimals="-5" name="ncmi:NegativeDistributionsMadeToLimitedLiabilityCompany" scale="6" id="f-707">19.6</ix:nonFraction> million for NCM, Inc.) and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i555d70cce26d468ca0c3486d4ca97e78_D20210101-20211230" decimals="-5" name="ncmi:NegativeDistributionsMadeToLimitedLiabilityCompany" scale="6" id="f-708">93.7</ix:nonFraction> million (including negative</span><span style="color:#ee2724;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"> </span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i192981ebfa524f5ba9cb557625a73913_D20210101-20211230" decimals="-5" name="ncmi:NegativeDistributionsMadeToLimitedLiabilityCompany" scale="6" id="f-709">24.3</ix:nonFraction> million for Cinemark, negative $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i40bc8fa51ec74911847f6368ecc44a9e_D20210101-20211230" decimals="-5" name="ncmi:NegativeDistributionsMadeToLimitedLiabilityCompany" scale="6" id="f-710">24.2</ix:nonFraction> million for Regal and negative</span><span style="color:#ee2724;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"> </span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="id211fde38efd480497e9b8cf558584a6_D20210101-20211230" decimals="-5" name="ncmi:NegativeDistributionsMadeToLimitedLiabilityCompany" scale="6" id="f-711">45.2</ix:nonFraction> million for NCM, Inc.) for the year ended December 30, 2021. Under the terms of the NCM LLC Operating Agreement, these negative amounts and the positive amounts above will be netted against each other and future positive available cash distributions after the Extended Covenant Waiver Holiday, contingent upon the Company's compliance with the Credit Agreement Second Amendment and the Credit Agreement Third Amendment defined within Note 10&#8212;Borrowings.&#160;</span></div><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="id6d0f0